# gameinput: Implement GameInputCreate and GetCurrentTimestamp.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12731 state=closed
# GameInputCreate() is currently a stub, so GDK games that read input through GameInput (Minecraft Bedrock, for one) get nothing back.

This adds a single shared GameInput object with the v0 and v2 interfaces, which are what the GDK and the current GameInput NuGet package ask for, and implements GetCurrentTimestamp(). I left out v1 since I haven't found anything that uses it. Everything else is still a stub; device enumeration and readings come in follow-up MRs.

The five v0 methods Microsoft documents as never implemented just return E_NOTIMPL with a TRACE, so they don't spam FIXMEs.

I tested on macOS with both 64-bit and 32-bit (wow64) builds. The new gameinput tests and dinput8's joystick8 pass, and each new test fails against a deliberately broken build.

### Not tested

- Windows, Linux.
